  "body": "Found while writing #339 slice 3 (fixture mesh for posed and C moves). Not yet reproduced as a missed hit, hence P1 pending a repro. It becomes P0 if a repro shows a real hit passing the post gate.\n\n**What the code does:** `cl::stamp_c` splits a turning (spindle-C) move into pieces that all keep the whole move's stated tool axis. On every piece but the last, that axis is off the live-tool station by the rest of the turn. The box fixture laws read the stated axis. For C moves they also judge on the part-frame chord, even for **fixed** steel, which stays in the machine frame. Either can put the judged tool stack somewhere other than where the machine puts it, so a real hit on fixed steel (a tailstock, a fixed clamp) could be missed.\n\n**Why #339's mesh law can't cover it:** it only ever clears box hits, so it cannot add the missing ones. Slice 3 reads C moves at the machine station for fixed steel, but only to clear hits. See `docs/decisions/339-mesh-posed.md` on the #339 branches.\n\n**Done means:**\n- A test with a C turning move past fixed steel near the station, judged by the box laws, reports the hit the machine would make; or a demonstration that it can't happen, with the reasoning pinned.\n- `stamp_c` pieces carry their own interpolated axis, or the laws read C moves in the machine frame for fixed steel.",
